---
// Legal and compliance. Company details come from site.ts; a row with an empty value is left out.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'company-details', title: 'Company details' },
  { id: 'regulatory-position', title: 'Regulatory position' },
  { id: 'gxp', title: 'GxP and data integrity' },
  { id: 'ai', title: 'Our position on AI' },
  { id: 'trademarks', title: 'Trademark notice' },
  { id: 'footage', title: 'Footage notice' },
  { id: 'anti-bribery', title: 'Anti-bribery' },
  { id: 'modern-slavery', title: 'Modern slavery' },
  { id: 'equal-opportunity', title: 'Equal opportunity' },
];

const details = [
  { term: 'Legal name', value: site.legalName },
  { term: 'Trading name', value: site.name },
  { term: 'Registered in', value: site.country },
  { term: 'Company number', value: site.croNumber },
  { term: 'Registered office', value: site.registeredOffice },
  { term: 'VAT number', value: site.vat },
  { term: 'Email', value: site.email, href: `mailto:${site.email}` },
  { term: 'Website', value: site.url.replace('https://', ''), href: site.url },
].filter((row) => row.value);
---

<Legal
  title="Legal and compliance: Viaclin"
  description="Company details for Viaclin Limited, our regulatory position as a consultancy, our stance on GxP, data integrity and AI, and notices on trademarks and footage."
  lead="Who Viaclin is in law, what we are and are not under medicines regulation, and the standards we hold ourselves to."
  path="/legal"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="company-details">Company details</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    {details.map((row) => (
      <div class="facts__row">
        <dt>{row.term}</dt>
        <dd>{row.href ? <a href={row.href}>{row.value}</a> : row.value}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 id="regulatory-position">Regulatory position</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin is a consultancy. We advise on, manage and improve clinical and commercial supply chains for life sciences
    companies.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Viaclin works as a consultancy. Where a programme needs a licence holder, for example a manufacturer, a
      wholesaler or an importer of record, the client or a contracted partner provides it under its own authorisation.
    </li>
    <li>
      Our work runs inside the client's quality system and under the client's licences, or those of the client's
      contracted partners. The licence holder keeps its regulatory duties at every stage.
    </li>
    <li>Batch certification and release stay with the Qualified Person named on the relevant licence.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site promotes a medicinal product, and nothing here is aimed at patients or the public as users of
    medicines. The site gives general information and not regulatory, quality, legal or medical advice. The
    {' '}<a href="/terms#no-professional-advice">terms of use</a> say more.
  </p>

  <h2 id="gxp">GxP and data integrity</h2>
  <p>
    Good practice rules exist to protect patients, and we treat them that way. On an engagement our consultants follow
    the client's procedures, complete the client's training before they touch a controlled process, and work in the
    client's validated systems with their own named accounts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Records we create or handle are kept attributable, legible, contemporaneous, original and accurate, and they stay
    complete, consistent, enduring and available. We do not keep shadow records outside the quality system. Deviations
    and errors are reported through the client's process, in the open and without delay.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">Our position on AI</h2>
  <p>
    Where AI is in scope, Optimised Operations work can include oversight agents, delivered with
    {' '}{site.sisterBrand.url
      ? <a href={site.sisterBrand.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">{site.sisterBrand.name}</a>
      : site.sisterBrand.name}. The position is simple:
    agents advise, people decide.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>An agent watches activity, flags risk and suggests a course of action. It does not act alone.</li>
    <li>A named person makes and owns every decision, including every GxP decision.</li>
    <li>
      AI enters a GxP workflow once its intended use, risks, controls and evidence are written down and the client's
      quality system has accepted them.
    </li>
    <li>Client data goes into an AI tool where the client has approved that tool for that data, and not before.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="trademarks">Trademark notice</h2>
  <p>
    Third-party names and logos on this site are trademarks of their owners. They appear in the consultant experience
    banner to describe the prior experience of consultants in the Viaclin network. No endorsement, sponsorship or
    partnership is suggested, and none should be inferred.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you own a mark shown here and want it changed or removed, email
    {' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will act on it.
  </p>
  <p>The Viaclin name, the V mark and the wordmark identify {site.legalName}.</p>

  <h2 id="footage">Footage notice</h2>
  <p>
    The films on this site are illustrative. They set the scene for each stage of a supply chain and do not show
    client sites or client products. The films carry no audio.
  </p>

  <h2 id="anti-bribery">Anti-bribery</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin does not offer, pay, ask for or accept bribes or facilitation payments, in any country, in person or
    through anyone who acts for us. We follow the Criminal Justice (Corruption Offences) Act 2018 and the equivalent
    law wherever we work. Gifts and hospitality stay modest, open and recorded. We expect the same of every consultant
    and supplier.
  </p>

  <h2 id="modern-slavery">Modern slavery</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin does not tolerate forced labour, child labour or human trafficking in its own business or in its supply
    chain. Consultants join us by choice and under written contracts. If we find a supplier that falls short, we raise
    it and, where it is not fixed, we end the relationship.
  </p>

  <h2 id="equal-opportunity">Equal opportunity</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin selects and treats consultants, staff and suppliers on merit. We do not discriminate on any of the nine
    grounds in Irish equality law: gender, civil status, family status, sexual orientation, religion, age, disability,
    race and membership of the Traveller community. We make reasonable accommodation for people with disabilities.
  </p>
</Legal>

<style>
  .facts {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .facts__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 4px 24px;
    padding: 14px clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 24px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .facts__row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .facts dt {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .facts__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
